           K_B = community_degrees[comm]  # note: K_B does not include i's degree\n                # but our community_degrees[current_comm] includes i's deg. For B, it does not.\n                sum_i_to_A = neigh_comm_sums[current_comm]\n                gain = (sum_to_comm - sum_i_to_A) / M - gamma * deg[node] * (K_B - K_A) / (2 * M * M)\n            if gain > best_gain or (gain == best_gain and comm < best_comm): # tie-break by community ID (string comparison)\n                best_gain = gain\n                best_comm = comm\n        if best_comm != current_comm and best_gain > 0: # strictly positive\n            # Move node\n            changes += 1\n            # Update community degrees\n            community_degrees[current_comm] -= deg[node]\n            community_degrees[best_comm] += deg[node]\n            # Update label\n            labels[node] = best_comm\n            # Record move\n            moves.append({\n                \"node\": node,\n                \"from\": current_comm,\n                \"to\": best_comm,\n                \"gain\": best_gain\n            })\n    # End pass; if changes==0, break.\n- Return {\"labels\": labels, \"move_ledger\": moves}\n\nWe must ensure the function is deterministic and uses only Python standard library.\n\nPotential issues: The community_degrees dict must include all communities from initial assignment, even if they become empty (no nodes). But we only care about communities that exist. After moving, some communities may become empty. We can leave them in community_degrees with value 0, but then later when a node evaluates gain for an empty community, K_B=0, sum_i_to_B=0, gain works. But we need to ensure we don't miss communities that have no nodes in current iteration (should not happen because we only evaluate communities that are neighbors of current node, which are non-empty by definition). However if a node has no neighbors, it will only have its own community, so no others.\n\nWe also need to handle floating point precision: Use float.\n\nEdge case: M could be zero if no edges? But edges list might be empty? The task doesn't specify, but assume at least some edges. Communities dictate nodes, but if no edges, no moves, degree 0 for all nodes, gain always 0, no moves. So return labels as is.\n\nNow test with given fixtures? Not required but verify logic.\n\nNow encode as JSON. The response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value containing Python source code as a string. The source must define `solve(case)`. We need to escape newlines, backslashes, and quotes. I'll write the code, then convert to JSON string.\n\nMake sure to import necessary modules (defaultdict). Use only standard lib.\n\nI'll produce the output."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1304,"completion_tokens":4814,"total_tokens":6118,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1024},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3972},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1024,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":280},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}